WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:41.300 align:middle line:90%


00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.110 align:middle line:90%
OK, Larry.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.100 align:middle line:90%
We're back.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.850 align:middle line:84%
And we'll start
again now I should

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.520 align:middle line:84%
say with your
experiences in Dachau.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.630 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, OK.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.440 align:middle line:84%
Dachau it was already
a more famous camp.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.430 align:middle line:90%
It was--

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.270 align:middle line:90%
It was a what camp?

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:56.990 align:middle line:90%
Famous.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:57.507 align:middle line:90%
Oh, famous.

00:00:57.507 --> 00:00:58.340 align:middle line:90%
I didn't understand.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.720 align:middle line:90%
More famous camp.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.910 align:middle line:90%
It was kept more and orderly.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.510 align:middle line:84%
There used to come international
visits from the Red Cross

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:06.380 align:middle line:90%
and from so.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.040 align:middle line:84%
So therefore, it was one
of the top-notch camps.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:11.870 align:middle line:90%
And it was kept.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.750 align:middle line:90%
How lucky you were there, right?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.150 align:middle line:90%
You ain't kidding.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.650 align:middle line:84%
That was compared with what's
been going on in other places,

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.483 align:middle line:90%
we were real lucky.

00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:20.150 align:middle line:90%
Can you imagine?

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.860 align:middle line:84%
So, but the luck
didn't last that long.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.500 align:middle line:84%
We stayed there for
three days, four days.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.480 align:middle line:84%
And then we were shipped from
there about a half a day's ride

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:35.690 align:middle line:84%
in a car, in a train near
Landsberg called Lager Seven.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.410 align:middle line:90%
Near Landsberg.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.820 align:middle line:90%
Landsberg is in what country?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.372 align:middle line:90%
In Germany.

00:01:38.372 --> 00:01:40.080 align:middle line:84%
That was in Germany,
not far from Dachau.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.120 align:middle line:84%
This was another work camp
you were being sent to.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.370 align:middle line:90%
Work camp, another lager, yes.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:47.260 align:middle line:84%
The same people that
you were with Warsaw.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.180 align:middle line:90%
In the Warsaw ghetto.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.350 align:middle line:84%
And who had made
the march with you?

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.160 align:middle line:90%
Whoever was left.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.220 align:middle line:84%
Yes, the same group that was
left from the Warsaw ghetto

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:53.910 align:middle line:90%
from there.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.380 align:middle line:90%
The 2,000 of you or whatever.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.010 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.870 align:middle line:84%
And the first one who were
there before I arrived,

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.540 align:middle line:90%
and the ones who came with me.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.715 align:middle line:84%
Whatever-- they needed a
certain number of workers?

00:02:02.715 --> 00:02:03.000 align:middle line:90%
Yes, right.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.500 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.830 align:middle line:90%
So we came back.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:05.580 align:middle line:90%
They took us.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.650 align:middle line:90%
We arrived in Landsberg.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:16.440 align:middle line:84%
Landsberg was in the ground,
so to speak, was underground.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.700 align:middle line:84%
It was built like the
Eskimos built their houses

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.530 align:middle line:90%
from ice, the same way.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.070 align:middle line:90%
Igloos.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:26.760 align:middle line:84%
Yes, the same way was
built, but made with--

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.360 align:middle line:90%
Earth.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.910 align:middle line:84%
Earth and the top and
green grass on it.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.620 align:middle line:90%
And we lived inside.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.450 align:middle line:84%
Inside there was plain wood and
straw, and you had a blanket,

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.320 align:middle line:90%
and that's it.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.780 align:middle line:84%
Landsberg was how far
from what big city?

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.030 align:middle line:90%
Do you know, have any idea?

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.270 align:middle line:84%
Landsberg in itself
is a big center point.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.840 align:middle line:90%
It's a big city in Germany.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.090 align:middle line:90%
Today it's still in existence?

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:47.960 align:middle line:90%
It still is, right.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.460 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.220 align:middle line:90%
That's number one.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.790 align:middle line:84%
And Landsberg, Hitler himself
was locked in, in that jail.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.510 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.560 align:middle line:90%
Not far from the Landsberg jail.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.315 align:middle line:84%
So I had the privilege of being
close to Hitler's own history.

00:03:00.315 --> 00:03:00.815 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:03:00.815 --> 00:03:04.400 align:middle line:90%


00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:11.120 align:middle line:84%
Being there for about five or
six weeks, typhus broke out.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.610 align:middle line:84%
So they quarantined
the whole camp.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.250 align:middle line:84%
Nobody could go in and
nobody could go out.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.520 align:middle line:84%
Do you have any idea how many
thousands were in this lager?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.660 align:middle line:90%
It's in the thousands.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.250 align:middle line:84%
I have no-- I have no
idea of the exact figure.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.460 align:middle line:84%
You mean nobody could go
out of his little hut?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.060 align:middle line:84%
No, out of our huts,
you could go out.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.560 align:middle line:90%
To work.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.430 align:middle line:90%
The camp, you couldn't--

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.540 align:middle line:90%
Couldn't leave to go to work.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.040 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.690 align:middle line:84%
It was sealed off
completely with them,

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.640 align:middle line:84%
that whoever will
survive will survive.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.260 align:middle line:90%
Whoever will die will die.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.490 align:middle line:84%
But after three days, they
decided to take a gamble.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.050 align:middle line:84%
And whoever was
still in good shape,

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.610 align:middle line:84%
they took him out
and see maybe they

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.690 align:middle line:90%
can use him somewhere to work.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.320 align:middle line:90%
So I still was good shape.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.420 align:middle line:84%
They took me out from
there and took me

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.460 align:middle line:90%
to a camp not far from there.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.470 align:middle line:84%
We walked, about three
hours walk called Kaufering,

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.880 align:middle line:90%
lager vier.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.090 align:middle line:84%
That's called means the
same camp like there was

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.950 align:middle line:90%
Landsberg, number seven.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.490 align:middle line:84%
Not far from there was a little
village called Kaufering.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.920 align:middle line:84%
And that was called
number camp number seven.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.420 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.410 align:middle line:84%
But it still belonged
to the same area.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:14.910 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:19.200 align:middle line:84%
So, and from there, we went to
work to the baustelle Holzmann.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.700 align:middle line:84%
Holzmann is a
German organization.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.330 align:middle line:84%
A baustelle, it's a
construction company

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.960 align:middle line:90%
that exists till this day.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:26.460 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.510 align:middle line:84%
So what kind of
work were you doing?

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.552 align:middle line:90%
So we went to work there.

00:04:28.552 --> 00:04:29.670 align:middle line:90%
We worked there at night.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:36.060 align:middle line:84%
For construction, building
underground airports, and stuff

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.950 align:middle line:90%
like that, construction work.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.360 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.050 align:middle line:84%
The food was lousy, and we
deteriorated it all of us.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:49.280 align:middle line:84%
And there one day, my father
couldn't go to work anymore.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.650 align:middle line:90%
My uncle, and all of that.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:55.670 align:middle line:84%
This particular older generation
couldn't take it anymore.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.392 align:middle line:90%
And they started to deteriorate.

00:04:57.392 --> 00:04:58.850 align:middle line:84%
Did you have any
idea about how old

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.350 align:middle line:90%
your father was at that time?

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.700 align:middle line:90%
At the time, 48.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.410 align:middle line:90%
But like an old man.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.390 align:middle line:84%
Completely broken,
completely old.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.970 align:middle line:84%
And he started to
deteriorate, and deteriorate,

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.210 align:middle line:84%
water in their knees,
water in their feet.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.614 align:middle line:84%
And one day, they came
in and took him away.

00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:16.820 align:middle line:90%
And that--

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.710 align:middle line:84%
That was the last
saw your father?

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.660 align:middle line:84%
One morning, I just said,
I'll see you tonight

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:21.770 align:middle line:90%
when I come back.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:22.910 align:middle line:90%
I left him in the camp.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:23.810 align:middle line:90%
I went to work.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:28.190 align:middle line:84%
I came back home, and he was
gone, not only him all of them,

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.150 align:middle line:84%
never to be seen,
never to be heard.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.810 align:middle line:84%
And I don't know how he
died or where he died,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.860 align:middle line:90%
and what he died.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:38.690 align:middle line:84%
But I assumed that he was taken
from there close to Dachau.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.410 align:middle line:84%
And he was thrown in and
he died somewhere in Dachau

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.030 align:middle line:84%
in the gas chamber or
something like that.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.510 align:middle line:84%
Were you-- now we
are in lager seven.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.690 align:middle line:90%
I mean lager four.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.640 align:middle line:90%
The Americans are approaching.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.410 align:middle line:90%
That the--

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.400 align:middle line:90%
You've heard rumors.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:02.240 align:middle line:84%
Rumors, we already know that
D-day took place a long time

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:02.780 align:middle line:90%
ago.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:04.250 align:middle line:90%
And this was already then.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.980 align:middle line:90%
That's already '44, close to--

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.630 align:middle line:90%


00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:14.840 align:middle line:84%
this is already not '44,
this is already '45.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:20.670 align:middle line:84%
That's already early spring,
late, late winter of '45.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:21.170 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.520 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.490 align:middle line:90%
We cannot go anymore to work.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.890 align:middle line:90%
I had typhus.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:33.240 align:middle line:84%
The camp was closed off,
no medication, no medicine.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.610 align:middle line:90%
I have typhus.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.770 align:middle line:84%
But I remember
the doctor telling

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.940 align:middle line:84%
me, if you get
ever get sick there

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.820 align:middle line:84%
is one thing what you
should do, try not

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.280 align:middle line:90%
to make dirt under yourself.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.280 align:middle line:90%
Stay clean as much as you can.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.290 align:middle line:90%
God knows I crawled on my feet.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.730 align:middle line:90%
I did everything.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:54.780 align:middle line:84%
And the only thing I
will forever never forget

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:59.010 align:middle line:84%
is I tried to crawl out
of my block, get out,

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.370 align:middle line:90%
and I crawled to the gate.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.870 align:middle line:84%
And I wanted to get
out of the gate.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.287 align:middle line:84%
And on the other
side of the gate,

00:07:05.287 --> 00:07:08.880 align:middle line:84%
there was a German,
two German guards, SS.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.070 align:middle line:84%
And one had his rifle
like this to my head.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:15.150 align:middle line:84%
And he says to
me, push the door.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.640 align:middle line:84%
If I push the door he
should be able to kill me.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.790 align:middle line:84%
So the other guard came
over to him and said,

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.980 align:middle line:90%
[GERMAN], leave him alone.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.040 align:middle line:90%
He says, exhaustion, fatigue.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.270 align:middle line:90%
He's already finished anyhow.

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:28.740 align:middle line:90%
Save yourself.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:29.880 align:middle line:90%
He was a little bit more--

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.000 align:middle line:90%
a little bit more humane.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.042 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, he says, leave him.

00:07:32.042 --> 00:07:33.720 align:middle line:90%
He is dead anyhow.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.670 align:middle line:90%
So save yourself the bullet.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.140 align:middle line:90%
Just leave him alone.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.308 align:middle line:84%
So and I broke down there,
and I fall down there.

00:07:41.308 --> 00:07:43.100 align:middle line:84%
I don't know for how
long I remained there.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.590 align:middle line:84%
But I mean remained
there and I lined up

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:50.330 align:middle line:84%
being back in my barrack, to be
shortly I made it in 28 days.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:54.920 align:middle line:84%
I had no food, no nothing, I
survived without medication,

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.000 align:middle line:90%
or without everything.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.737 align:middle line:90%
I'm here, thank God.

00:07:57.737 --> 00:07:58.820 align:middle line:90%
What do you get with this?

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:00.650 align:middle line:90%
What do you mean 28 days?

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:01.280 align:middle line:90%
Until--

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.190 align:middle line:84%
28 days I was out of
food, out of water.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:04.910 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I see.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.140 align:middle line:90%
Out of medication.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.220 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.610 align:middle line:84%
With being the way
I was, high fever.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:14.090 align:middle line:84%
Then actually you were
liberated at that point?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:19.220 align:middle line:84%
Then one morning we
woke up, and they

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.950 align:middle line:84%
said they are going
to evacuate us again.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.630 align:middle line:84%
We had to go out
of the barracks.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:24.830 align:middle line:90%
We got out of the barracks.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:25.820 align:middle line:90%
As sick as you were?

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:28.220 align:middle line:84%
As sick as we were, we
just schlepped on our feet,

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:29.030 align:middle line:90%
and all that.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.580 align:middle line:84%
We have been sitting
there outside and waiting.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:34.880 align:middle line:84%
Finally, we helped each
other to crawl in the trains.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.346 align:middle line:84%
And they were, again,
taking us God knows where.

00:08:37.346 --> 00:08:38.929 align:middle line:84%
I don't know where
they were taking us

00:08:38.929 --> 00:08:40.740 align:middle line:90%
from one place to the other.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.679 align:middle line:84%
The Air Force came in,
the American Air Force.

00:08:43.679 --> 00:08:46.350 align:middle line:90%
They shot the locomotive out.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.240 align:middle line:90%
They shot the locomotive out.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.500 align:middle line:90%
So the train couldn't move.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:53.500 align:middle line:90%
And we were stuck on the track.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.390 align:middle line:84%
And as we were
stuck on the track,

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.580 align:middle line:84%
and they started
to bomb the track,

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:04.440 align:middle line:84%
I only remember that
somehow I jumped over

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.790 align:middle line:90%
from the inside out.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.020 align:middle line:84%
It was like a coal,
they're transporting

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.670 align:middle line:90%
coal, and that kind of--

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:12.330 align:middle line:90%
It was open.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.290 align:middle line:90%
It was open on the top.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:13.790 align:middle line:90%
On the top.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:14.300 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:14.940 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:15.840 align:middle line:90%
That kind of--

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.250 align:middle line:90%
So you were able to jump over.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:20.910 align:middle line:84%
Right, I jumped over, and I fall
down, and I opened up the door.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.870 align:middle line:84%
And we opened it up so the
inside started to escape.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.650 align:middle line:84%
And the ones that started
to run away, all of a sudden

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:29.730 align:middle line:90%
started to be shot at.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.280 align:middle line:84%
We didn't know from where
then I looked around,

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.330 align:middle line:84%
and I realized what happened
we came in a two way lane.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.170 align:middle line:84%
And next to us stopped
an army train loaded

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.810 align:middle line:84%
with soldiers and
with flags, with fire,

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.520 align:middle line:84%
you know anti-aircraft
fire and all of.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.100 align:middle line:90%
That.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.223 align:middle line:90%
And they thought that if--

00:09:46.223 --> 00:09:46.890 align:middle line:90%
The German army?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.490 align:middle line:84%
Yes, the trains will come and
see that we are who we are,

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.170 align:middle line:84%
they we will not
bomb them, and then

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.780 align:middle line:84%
they will be able to
retaliate and shoot.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.240 align:middle line:90%
So they used us as an escape.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.270 align:middle line:90%
Almost like a hostage.

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.730 align:middle line:90%
A hostage, right.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.200 align:middle line:84%
But as soon I realized
what happened,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.260 align:middle line:84%
and I told some of
my boys, I still

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:09.010 align:middle line:84%
had original from we started
out eight from my hardcore,

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.260 align:middle line:90%
you remember in the beginning.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:10.890 align:middle line:90%
Right, but they were--

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:11.610 align:middle line:90%
There were three left.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.150 align:middle line:90%
Only three.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.530 align:middle line:90%
Together three.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:14.625 align:middle line:90%
Myself, and two more.

00:10:14.625 --> 00:10:16.260 align:middle line:90%
There were three left.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.190 align:middle line:84%
The other ones got killed,
died, and that's it.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:21.900 align:middle line:90%
Typhus took some of them.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.430 align:middle line:90%
And were only three left.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.495 align:middle line:90%
We got together.

00:10:24.495 --> 00:10:28.136 align:middle line:90%


00:10:28.136 --> 00:10:31.680 align:middle line:84%
I don't want to go in again
on something on that because.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.690 align:middle line:84%
It will sound like
I'm always the hero

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.450 align:middle line:84%
and always something can
happen, and I'm always doing

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.780 align:middle line:90%
something for somebody else.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:38.490 align:middle line:90%
A girl gets shot.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.907 align:middle line:84%
OK, so the three
of you were left.

00:10:39.907 --> 00:10:40.500 align:middle line:90%
And did you--

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.990 align:middle line:90%
And some of them got away.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.740 align:middle line:84%
You got away, the three
of you and others.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.150 align:middle line:84%
We got away, we run
away in the forest.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:45.650 align:middle line:90%
We run away.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.280 align:middle line:84%
There was a little
forest we got in.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.590 align:middle line:84%
And it poured and
rained outside.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:51.150 align:middle line:90%
And we stayed there.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:56.340 align:middle line:84%
We found some ammunition
guns that the German ,

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:01.140 align:middle line:84%
army the soldiers threw away
from themselves, and you know.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.480 align:middle line:84%
And finally the next
day in the morning

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:07.650 align:middle line:84%
we went in a little small
village called Schwabhausen,

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:10.170 align:middle line:84%
and there we seen
the American army.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.310 align:middle line:90%
We were liberated.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.760 align:middle line:84%
As soon as we saw the Americans,
the first thing the said to us,

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.440 align:middle line:90%
sit down and stay here.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.900 align:middle line:84%
You were still in
this prison clothing.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:22.830 align:middle line:84%
Prison clothing, all that, all
walking like-- they recognized

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.160 align:middle line:90%
it right away who we are.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:24.660 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.010 align:middle line:90%
Well you had to be terrible.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:26.520 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yeah.

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:30.480 align:middle line:84%
Well I weighed--
what did I weigh?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.070 align:middle line:90%
38 kilos.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.850 align:middle line:84%
What does it mean
38, kilos is what?

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.560 align:middle line:84%
About two kilos to
a pound I think,

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:41.860 align:middle line:84%
Yeah so about 20 pounds or 25
pounds, complete skin and bone.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:46.450 align:middle line:84%
I just crawled you could
see everything on me.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.550 align:middle line:84%
Just like you see it in
the picture, when you see.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.818 align:middle line:90%
That's exactly the way I looked.

00:11:50.818 --> 00:11:52.360 align:middle line:84%
Did you think that
you would survive?

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:53.800 align:middle line:90%
No, I didn't believe it.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.660 align:middle line:90%
What gave you strength and hope?

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:58.780 align:middle line:84%
Well, the strength,
like I said, you

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.300 align:middle line:84%
remember in the beginning
I said that kept me.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.970 align:middle line:84%
And I said, nothing is going
nothing's going to break me.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:07.990 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to survive no
matter what under any kind

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.250 align:middle line:90%
of circumstances.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.495 align:middle line:84%
And they got me
into the hospital.

00:12:11.495 --> 00:12:12.370 align:middle line:90%
Wonderful, wonderful.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.630 align:middle line:90%
And at the hospital--

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:16.150 align:middle line:84%
Hospital there, an American
Hospital in Germany?

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.740 align:middle line:90%
Yes, an army hospital.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:18.730 align:middle line:90%
They took us in.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.710 align:middle line:84%
The first thing they
cleaned us, of course,

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.760 align:middle line:90%
and they checked us out.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:29.860 align:middle line:84%
And the first, the
second meal is a story

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.860 align:middle line:84%
to be seen, or be
told in itself.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:36.760 align:middle line:84%
And in the way by knowing
that the food is here,

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:39.700 align:middle line:84%
and even knowing the
food will be served,

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:42.850 align:middle line:84%
and when the nurses came
in and served the bed here

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.910 align:middle line:84%
for the guy, that the
guy on the end of the bed

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.760 align:middle line:84%
jumped out and ran over
here, and grabbed the food.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.590 align:middle line:84%
Afraid that he
wouldn't get his share.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:53.110 align:middle line:90%
A raid, like a raid.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:56.230 align:middle line:90%
This is when I broke down.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.090 align:middle line:90%
This is when I cried.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:01.090 align:middle line:90%
And I had a 50, the only--

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.610 align:middle line:84%
well, 50 years take or
give a little bit older,

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:11.080 align:middle line:84%
the only older guy who
survived with us at this point,

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:14.990 align:middle line:90%
he was six years in the camps.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.480 align:middle line:90%
And he survived.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.120 align:middle line:84%
And he was the
only one till then.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:19.790 align:middle line:90%
This was all--

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:21.790 align:middle line:84%
And we both-- this is
already after the break.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:22.920 align:middle line:90%
1945.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:23.558 align:middle line:90%
That's in 1945.

00:13:23.558 --> 00:13:24.100 align:middle line:90%
This is when?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:24.840 align:middle line:90%
May, in May.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.490 align:middle line:90%
May, all right.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.830 align:middle line:90%
And you're in the hospital.

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:30.070 align:middle line:90%
Yes that's May whatever.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.410 align:middle line:84%
Yeah that's in May,
right in month of May.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.460 align:middle line:90%
We are in the hospital.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.360 align:middle line:90%
We are liberated.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.943 align:middle line:84%
And how old at this time, you're
almost-- you're 20 years old.

00:13:36.943 --> 00:13:38.200 align:middle line:90%
I'm already now 20 years old.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:38.470 align:middle line:90%
Right, OK.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:39.590 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, it's one month before--

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.120 align:middle line:90%
And you've lived a lifetime.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:40.620 align:middle line:90%
Right?

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:43.790 align:middle line:84%
That's one month before
my 20th birthday.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:44.800 align:middle line:90%
I was born in June.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.550 align:middle line:84%
June is my birthday, so was one
month before my 20th birthday.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.250 align:middle line:90%
And he is crying and I'm crying.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:54.080 align:middle line:84%
We are happy, but
yet what he says,

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.458 align:middle line:90%
look what he made out of us.

00:13:55.458 --> 00:13:56.500 align:middle line:90%
The food is here already.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.530 align:middle line:90%
We are liberated.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.380 align:middle line:90%
We are still like animals.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.230 align:middle line:84%
And I woke up the next
morning sleeping next to him.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:05.630 align:middle line:84%
I want to call him, and I see
his laying with his hand down.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.120 align:middle line:90%
So I thought maybe he feels.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:07.870 align:middle line:90%
The man died.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.350 align:middle line:90%
He had a heart attack.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.270 align:middle line:90%
The doctor told me.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:11.860 align:middle line:90%
How old was this man?

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.210 align:middle line:90%
Your age, young man.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.720 align:middle line:90%
He was in his close to 50.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:16.570 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I see.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:17.980 align:middle line:90%
He was the only older guy.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.780 align:middle line:90%
I'm young for my age.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:22.240 align:middle line:84%
The doctor told me he
died of a heart attack

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.780 align:middle line:84%
because he says the concept
of being free after six years.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:27.280 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:27.970 align:middle line:90%
That's--

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:28.900 align:middle line:90%
Just couldn't take it.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.700 align:middle line:90%
Couldn't take it, and he died.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.440 align:middle line:90%
OK, then you're liberated.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.057 align:middle line:90%
Now, where did you go?

00:14:35.057 --> 00:14:36.640 align:middle line:84%
How long did you
stay in the hospital?

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.080 align:middle line:84%
How long did it take
you to recuperate?

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.163 align:middle line:84%
I stayed in the hospital
for about a month's time.

00:14:40.163 --> 00:14:42.520 align:middle line:84%
In June, they transported
us back to Czechoslovakia.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.230 align:middle line:90%
They asked who wants to go back.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.910 align:middle line:90%
Of course, the war is over.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.980 align:middle line:84%
Czechoslovakia is
Czechoslovakia.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.720 align:middle line:90%
I went back to Czechoslovakia.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.760 align:middle line:84%
You went home to look--
try to find family.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:52.600 align:middle line:90%
I'm not home yet.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.410 align:middle line:90%
I'm in-- I'm in Prague.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:59.410 align:middle line:84%
And in Prague I met girls
who came from Germany,

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.740 align:middle line:84%
from my hometown, and they
told me that my sister is alive

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.130 align:middle line:84%
and she is in Bergen-Belsen
in the British zone,

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.300 align:middle line:90%
the British occupation.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.210 align:middle line:90%
And she is there.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.660 align:middle line:90%
She's been liberated.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:13.360 align:middle line:84%
Right, and she is there
and that she is alive.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.100 align:middle line:84%
So now, I know my
sister is alive.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.735 align:middle line:90%
This is one sister of four.

00:15:16.735 --> 00:15:20.510 align:middle line:84%
Four, and the rest of
them I didn't even count.

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:23.560 align:middle line:84%
I haven't counted on her
either, but somehow she managed.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.137 align:middle line:84%
Because she was
already 14 years old.

00:15:25.137 --> 00:15:26.470 align:middle line:90%
And the other ones were younger?

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:26.920 align:middle line:90%
One younger.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.460 align:middle line:84%
Were you the oldest
in your family, Larry?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:29.080 align:middle line:90%
I was the oldest in the family.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:29.560 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:30.060 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:33.790 align:middle line:90%


00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.830 align:middle line:90%
I'm in Czechoslovakia.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.270 align:middle line:90%
I meet with my boys.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.230 align:middle line:84%
I found from the two
boys who survived

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:44.790 align:middle line:84%
with me, we are three from
our original gang of 16,

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.650 align:middle line:90%
four more is available.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.140 align:middle line:84%
And one more we found
later on another one.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:51.120 align:middle line:84%
We are becoming again
a group of eight.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.670 align:middle line:90%
Half of us survived.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:57.090 align:middle line:84%
We decide we are going
to go home and take

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.920 align:middle line:90%
a look what's going on at home.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.540 align:middle line:84%
So of us say they
don't want to go.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:04.380 align:middle line:84%
I decided I'm going to go
just for one more time.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.790 align:middle line:90%
I went.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.280 align:middle line:84%
I wish I would be
a poet or a writer

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.280 align:middle line:84%
to describe the
feelings, and how it was,

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.640 align:middle line:84%
and what it just went through,
village after village,

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:18.270 align:middle line:84%
small town after
small town, empty.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:22.320 align:middle line:90%
No Jewish life, no death.

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:25.620 align:middle line:90%
No houses destroyed, empty.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:28.710 align:middle line:84%
You know, like
nature takes his tool

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:32.760 align:middle line:84%
on emptiness, and all of that
grass growing everywhere,

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.950 align:middle line:90%
no nothing.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:38.430 align:middle line:90%
It's '45 fall.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.920 align:middle line:90%
I leave home.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:41.860 align:middle line:90%
I'm on my way to Budapest.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:45.430 align:middle line:84%
Now, you will be
able to understand

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.580 align:middle line:84%
on the beginning what
I wasn't able to say,

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:52.110 align:middle line:84%
because it didn't work out
as now you will understand.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:52.610 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:53.200 align:middle line:90%
Here--

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.200 align:middle line:90%
So you went to Budapest.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.300 align:middle line:90%
It's '45.

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:58.840 align:middle line:84%
In Budapest I meet
with Joel Brand.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:03.760 align:middle line:84%
This is the same Joel Brand
that dealt with Eichmann before.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.490 align:middle line:90%
I saw Eichmann in 1943.

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.130 align:middle line:84%
But I didn't know who
he is at the time.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.089 align:middle line:90%
Where did you see him?

00:17:10.089 --> 00:17:11.950 align:middle line:90%
In Budapest.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.960 align:middle line:90%
Oh before the-- this was before?

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.150 align:middle line:90%
Before the arrest, right?

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.740 align:middle line:90%
To me, we saw.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.119 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know his name.

00:17:19.119 --> 00:17:23.000 align:middle line:84%
I saw an SS man, but an
officer, a German SS officer.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.250 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know who he is.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.750 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know what it meant.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.849 align:middle line:84%
Eichmann didn't mean
nothing to me at the time.

00:17:27.849 --> 00:17:28.540 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.460 align:middle line:90%
Now it meant everything already.

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.430 align:middle line:90%
We knew already, and Joel Brand.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.470 align:middle line:84%
You mean in 1945
you knew already?

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.340 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.030 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:40.290 align:middle line:84%
We had a long talk
with Joel Brand.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:46.080 align:middle line:84%
And Joel Brand told me
then, and he says someday we

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.540 align:middle line:90%
will be in Israel.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.920 align:middle line:90%
Israel will be liberated.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.150 align:middle line:90%
And we'll be able to talk.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:55.890 align:middle line:84%
Right now, our main
objective is to get,

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.240 align:middle line:90%
to create the state of Israel.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:58.740 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.170 align:middle line:90%
So this is from Budapest.

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.190 align:middle line:90%
Then where did you go?

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:07.770 align:middle line:84%
In Budapest, there were
transports leaving for Italy

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.780 align:middle line:90%
and back to Germany.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:14.700 align:middle line:84%
I decided my first priority is
to go back and see my sister.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:18.450 align:middle line:84%
She doesn't know that I'm
alive but I do know about her

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.250 align:middle line:84%
So you're going to I
wrote a letter here

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.100 align:middle line:84%
to America to my uncle from
Germany from the hospital.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.440 align:middle line:84%
There was a doctor,
a Jewish doctor

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:29.100 align:middle line:84%
who was in the army
who came to visit.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.300 align:middle line:90%
I don't this.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:32.190 align:middle line:90%
This is I'm finding out later.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.350 align:middle line:84%
He says, he asked if anybody
has family in America.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:38.490 align:middle line:84%
And I said yes, I have an
uncle by the name of Janowitz,

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.510 align:middle line:90%
and he lives in Cleveland, Ohio.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:41.860 align:middle line:90%
That's all I know.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.187 align:middle line:90%
So he took the name.

00:18:43.187 --> 00:18:44.020 align:middle line:90%
He took the address.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.540 align:middle line:90%
He came back to the States.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.190 align:middle line:90%
He looked up at the telephone.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:52.270 align:middle line:84%
He found my uncle, the
address, he called him up.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:54.610 align:middle line:84%
Later, years later,
my uncle tells me

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.580 align:middle line:84%
he gets a call on
a Saturday night.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:00.910 align:middle line:84%
The man on the other line
introduces himself as Rabbi

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.730 align:middle line:90%
so and so.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.670 align:middle line:84%
And he says, I have
a message for you

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.340 align:middle line:90%
by the name of Leibi Hersch.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:10.720 align:middle line:84%
And he is your
sister's son, Leah.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:11.530 align:middle line:90%
The son.

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:13.390 align:middle line:90%
That he is a survivor.

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:16.780 align:middle line:84%
He is the only thing that
he knows he is alive.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.550 align:middle line:84%
He is going to go
home to look around.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.950 align:middle line:84%
He doesn't know who
survived or who didn't.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.550 align:middle line:84%
But my sister already did the
same thing with somebody else.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:26.020 align:middle line:90%
And he already knew.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.490 align:middle line:84%
He already was in
correspondence with my sister.

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:30.040 align:middle line:90%
But I don't know all of that.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:30.880 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:33.130 align:middle line:90%
Now I'm leaving Budapest.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.620 align:middle line:90%
I'm on my way to Prague.

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:39.040 align:middle line:84%
In Prague, I meet
one of my friends.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.110 align:middle line:84%
How do you get to
these different places?

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:41.770 align:middle line:90%
Just by train.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:42.730 align:middle line:90%
Jump on a train and go.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:44.730 align:middle line:84%
Oh, were there trains
were running at that time?

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:46.240 align:middle line:84%
Running trains,
yeah loaded to top.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.230 align:middle line:90%
Everybody's running around.

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:48.100 align:middle line:90%
Everybody's running around.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:48.760 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, OK.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.660 align:middle line:90%
I jump on a train take Budapest.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.710 align:middle line:84%
I ate breakfast here,
supper I already

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.218 align:middle line:84%
had in a different
country, if I had supper.

00:19:56.218 --> 00:19:58.510 align:middle line:84%
But I had a piece of bread
what you could put together.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.065 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:19:59.065 --> 00:20:04.690 align:middle line:84%
In Prague, I meet one of the
boys who went in '42 and in '43

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:06.430 align:middle line:90%
for Aliyah to Palestine.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.190 align:middle line:84%
He is with the
Jewish Bricha back.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.870 align:middle line:90%
He came back.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:15.400 align:middle line:84%
He says, Larry,
big hug, you know.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.080 align:middle line:90%
I got a job for you.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:18.220 align:middle line:90%
For me?

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:19.270 align:middle line:90%
Come with me.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.190 align:middle line:90%
He took me away.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:24.850 align:middle line:84%
I became a member of the
Irgun right there and then.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.160 align:middle line:90%
That was the top.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:31.720 align:middle line:84%
And I started to work
for the Irgun from there.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.235 align:middle line:90%
There or you went to Israel?

00:20:33.235 --> 00:20:34.360 align:middle line:90%
With the Bricha.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:36.580 align:middle line:84%
First, my job was,
because the fact

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.935 align:middle line:84%
that I spoke all
those languages,

00:20:38.935 --> 00:20:42.670 align:middle line:84%
is I used to bring transport
let's say to smuggle them out

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.580 align:middle line:84%
between the Hungarian
border to Austria,

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.620 align:middle line:84%
from the Polish
border to Austria,

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.500 align:middle line:84%
from Czechoslovakia to
Austria, or to Germany,

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:51.723 align:middle line:90%
all dependent on what it was.

00:20:51.723 --> 00:20:53.140 align:middle line:84%
So how many years
did you do that?

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:58.990 align:middle line:84%
I worked in that
from '45 till '47.

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:01.180 align:middle line:90%
Two years.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:05.650 align:middle line:84%
In the beginning of '47
I left for Palestine.

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:07.540 align:middle line:90%
I became active.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:08.665 align:middle line:90%
How did you make that trip?

00:21:08.665 --> 00:21:11.390 align:middle line:90%


00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:14.455 align:middle line:84%
On what you called
Aliyah Bet, which

00:21:14.455 --> 00:21:18.458 align:middle line:84%
is called Aliyah Bet
is the secret, the--

00:21:18.458 --> 00:21:19.000 align:middle line:90%
Well, I know.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.260 align:middle line:90%
But did you travel by train?

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.400 align:middle line:90%
Did you travel by ship?

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:21.880 align:middle line:90%
No, no, no, by ship.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:22.525 align:middle line:90%
By ship.

00:21:22.525 --> 00:21:23.550 align:middle line:90%
You went in the Mediterranean.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.550 align:middle line:90%
Mediterranean, from Italy, yes.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:25.090 align:middle line:90%
So you had to go down.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:26.460 align:middle line:84%
Oh, you were in
Italy at that time.

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:26.960 align:middle line:90%
OK, fine.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:31.100 align:middle line:84%
From Italy, and from Italy
we went to on a little boat.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.800 align:middle line:90%
So how long did that take?

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:34.150 align:middle line:90%
It take me 10 days.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:34.820 align:middle line:90%
That's all.

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:35.320 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:38.510 align:middle line:90%
I was in Israel, in Palestine.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:42.740 align:middle line:84%
I was active in different
things with the Irgun.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:50.120 align:middle line:84%
And with eight months
later, rumors already

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.130 align:middle line:84%
that the state of
Israel will be created.

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.420 align:middle line:90%
It's just a matter of time.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:56.880 align:middle line:90%


00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:01.640 align:middle line:84%
The United Nations voted for
it, and all of that activity

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:02.280 align:middle line:90%
going on.

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:05.570 align:middle line:84%
So it was already a fact
that the state of Israel,

00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:07.290 align:middle line:90%
just a matter of time.

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:11.090 align:middle line:84%
But in the meantime, somehow the
British got hold of my picture

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:12.830 align:middle line:90%
in Germany.

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:14.540 align:middle line:90%
And they knew who I was.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:17.910 align:middle line:84%
So the decision was made instead
of them to get hold of me,

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:19.160 align:middle line:90%
they have been looking for me.

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:21.590 align:middle line:84%
I had to leave once
more Palestine.

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:24.260 align:middle line:90%
So I was smuggled out on a boat.

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:25.250 align:middle line:90%
I had to walk in.

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:26.900 align:middle line:90%
I was put in a--

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:30.080 align:middle line:90%


00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:33.410 align:middle line:90%
between oranges and grapefruit.

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:33.950 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:34.850 align:middle line:90%
And put in a hole.

00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:35.510 align:middle line:90%
To go where?

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:38.060 align:middle line:84%
And I went, the best
way for me was not

00:22:38.060 --> 00:22:41.460 align:middle line:84%
to go anywhere else, just
to go direct to the British.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:44.830 align:middle line:84%
So I went from
Palestine to Cyprus.

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:45.330 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:47.300 align:middle line:84%
And let me just interrupt
you for a minute.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:49.220 align:middle line:84%
Direct to the British
in their own mouth.

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:50.510 align:middle line:90%
You went back.

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:53.870 align:middle line:84%
You told me that you actually
before you got involved

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:54.843 align:middle line:90%
in this, you went back.

00:22:54.843 --> 00:22:56.510 align:middle line:84%
It was your choice
to go back to Germany

00:22:56.510 --> 00:22:57.320 align:middle line:90%
to look for your sister.

00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:57.680 align:middle line:90%
I went back to Germany.

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:58.560 align:middle line:90%
Did you find her?

00:22:58.560 --> 00:22:59.060 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:22:59.957 align:middle line:90%
I found my sister.

00:22:59.957 --> 00:23:01.040 align:middle line:90%
And then you said goodbye.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:01.550 align:middle line:90%
I'm going to go.

00:23:01.550 --> 00:23:04.160 align:middle line:84%
I said to my sister, yeah, I
had things to do, as long as I--

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:06.420 align:middle line:84%
she knew that I'm alive,
and she knew that I'm alive.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:06.920 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:07.580 align:middle line:90%
And--

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:10.260 align:middle line:84%
She was probably in a displaced
persons camp or something

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:10.760 align:middle line:90%
at the time.

00:23:10.760 --> 00:23:13.280 align:middle line:90%
Yes, she was in a DP camp.

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:16.320 align:middle line:90%
And she left to America in 1947.

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:16.820 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:17.300 align:middle line:90%
She came to America.

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:19.258 align:middle line:84%
You had no more contact
with her at that point.

00:23:19.258 --> 00:23:21.350 align:middle line:84%
Just writing, but when
I was in Palestine.

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:23.540 align:middle line:84%
I didn't write her
anything, we didn't.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:24.650 align:middle line:90%
No contact at all.

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:27.180 align:middle line:84%
My uncle once in a while
he used to drop a letter.

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:29.660 align:middle line:84%
But I didn't want them
to send me anything.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:30.720 align:middle line:90%
Because for give away.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:31.470 align:middle line:90%
Right, subversive.

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:32.240 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:34.400 align:middle line:90%
Then I was smuggled out.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:37.400 align:middle line:90%
I went to Cyprus on a boat.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:42.670 align:middle line:84%
And from the same boat, I went
back all the way to France.

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:45.530 align:middle line:84%
And from France, I was
taken back to Germany.

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:49.480 align:middle line:90%
So I left in 1947.

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:58.550 align:middle line:84%
Sometimes it would be by the
end of May, I left in '47.

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:04.940 align:middle line:84%
By February of '48, I
was back in Germany.

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:08.150 align:middle line:84%
OK, now let's just skip
over some of these years.

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:11.610 align:middle line:84%
And tell us when you
came to this country.

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:12.860 align:middle line:90%
When did you come to America--

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:14.600 align:middle line:90%
I came to America in '56.

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.250 align:middle line:90%
--or to the US or to Cleveland?

00:24:16.250 --> 00:24:18.500 align:middle line:90%
Cleveland, I came in 1956.

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:21.770 align:middle line:84%
After that eight year period
then, what did you do?

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:23.970 align:middle line:84%
You were working for
the Irgun all this time?

00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:24.560 align:middle line:90%
No, no, no.

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:27.680 align:middle line:84%
The Irgun dissolved in 1948
after the establishment

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:30.080 align:middle line:90%
of the State of Israel.

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:33.740 align:middle line:84%
When I was in Germany and in
'48, at the beginning of '48,

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:36.200 align:middle line:84%
I was active with the Irgun
doing different things

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:38.090 align:middle line:90%
at different places.

00:24:38.090 --> 00:24:42.320 align:middle line:84%
In '48, I received the
standard order to report back,

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:45.110 align:middle line:84%
coming back to
Israel, which if you

00:24:45.110 --> 00:24:47.900 align:middle line:84%
remember the story
with the boat Altalena.

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:51.890 align:middle line:84%
That boat came and was in
confrontation with Ben-Gurion,

00:24:51.890 --> 00:24:53.840 align:middle line:90%
and with the army at the time.

00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:57.720 align:middle line:84%
So I came back on the
Altalena, and after there, we

00:24:57.720 --> 00:25:01.260 align:middle line:90%
were ending to the army.

00:25:01.260 --> 00:25:02.032 align:middle line:90%
I joined the army.

00:25:02.032 --> 00:25:03.240 align:middle line:90%
You were in the Israeli army.

00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:05.100 align:middle line:84%
The Israeli army,
and stayed there.

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:09.840 align:middle line:84%
I stayed in the Israeli army for
eight years, till the 1956 war.

00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:11.610 align:middle line:90%
Oh, the Six-Day War.

00:25:11.610 --> 00:25:12.600 align:middle line:90%
In '56.

00:25:12.600 --> 00:25:13.750 align:middle line:90%
Was that the Six-Day War?

00:25:13.750 --> 00:25:17.850 align:middle line:84%
No, no, '67 was the Six-Day
War. '56 was another thing.

00:25:17.850 --> 00:25:19.120 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:19.620 align:middle line:90%
Excuse me.

00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:23.340 align:middle line:84%
After the '56 war,
I came to America.

00:25:23.340 --> 00:25:24.100 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:25:24.100 --> 00:25:24.900 align:middle line:90%
In America--

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:26.640 align:middle line:90%
How did you come here?

00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:28.740 align:middle line:84%
I came to my sister
who was here already.

00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:29.790 align:middle line:90%
She was married.

00:25:29.790 --> 00:25:32.410 align:middle line:84%
Did she-- did you need help
to come here at that time?

00:25:32.410 --> 00:25:35.910 align:middle line:84%
Oh, yes, well but no, no
organization or anything

00:25:35.910 --> 00:25:37.710 align:middle line:90%
of this nature, no help.

00:25:37.710 --> 00:25:39.510 align:middle line:84%
It came from my own
family, from my--

00:25:39.510 --> 00:25:40.290 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:25:40.290 --> 00:25:41.130 align:middle line:90%
No--

00:25:41.130 --> 00:25:42.450 align:middle line:90%
No religious organization--

00:25:42.450 --> 00:25:43.260 align:middle line:90%
No religious organization.

00:25:43.260 --> 00:25:44.460 align:middle line:90%
--welcomed you or anything.

00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:46.030 align:middle line:84%
Because you had
family here already.

00:25:46.030 --> 00:25:46.530 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:25:46.530 --> 00:25:48.090 align:middle line:90%
OK, it was your sister.

00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:50.130 align:middle line:84%
She was here already
too by my uncle.

00:25:50.130 --> 00:25:51.300 align:middle line:90%
She came to my uncle.

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:52.830 align:middle line:90%
My uncle took her out and all.

00:25:52.830 --> 00:25:53.760 align:middle line:90%
He paid for her.

00:25:53.760 --> 00:25:56.200 align:middle line:84%
This was this Mr. Janowitz
who lived in Cleveland.

00:25:56.200 --> 00:25:56.700 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:25:56.700 --> 00:25:59.220 align:middle line:90%
And he saw that she got here.

00:25:59.220 --> 00:25:59.730 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:25:59.730 --> 00:26:00.010 align:middle line:90%
He took her our.

00:26:00.010 --> 00:26:00.870 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:26:00.870 --> 00:26:02.550 align:middle line:90%
And she stayed in their house.

00:26:02.550 --> 00:26:07.740 align:middle line:84%
And they just took her in
one of their own daughters.

00:26:07.740 --> 00:26:11.670 align:middle line:90%
So you came here in '56.

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:14.370 align:middle line:84%
At that time, so you were
not married then, you said.

00:26:14.370 --> 00:26:16.080 align:middle line:84%
No, at that time
I wasn't married.

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:16.740 align:middle line:90%
I married.

00:26:16.740 --> 00:26:18.790 align:middle line:90%
I met my wife here in Cleveland.

00:26:18.790 --> 00:26:21.480 align:middle line:84%
Did you live with your uncle
and your sister when you came?

00:26:21.480 --> 00:26:23.130 align:middle line:90%
Yes, I stayed with my uncle.

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:25.110 align:middle line:84%
First, I stayed with my
sister for a few days,

00:26:25.110 --> 00:26:26.520 align:middle line:84%
and then I moved
in with my uncle

00:26:26.520 --> 00:26:28.240 align:middle line:84%
because all of their
children were gone.

00:26:28.240 --> 00:26:29.610 align:middle line:90%
And they had a big house.

00:26:29.610 --> 00:26:33.040 align:middle line:84%
So I moved in there for
the first three months.

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:36.250 align:middle line:84%
And then after I found work, I
moved out of there on my own.

00:26:36.250 --> 00:26:37.050 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:26:37.050 --> 00:26:40.590 align:middle line:84%
In general, did people
want to learn about what

00:26:40.590 --> 00:26:41.800 align:middle line:90%
you had gone through?

00:26:41.800 --> 00:26:42.300 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:43.890 align:middle line:90%
Nobody was really interested.

00:26:43.890 --> 00:26:46.650 align:middle line:90%
Nobody was interested.

00:26:46.650 --> 00:26:50.520 align:middle line:84%
In two ways, I think
it's a two-way street.

00:26:50.520 --> 00:26:55.853 align:middle line:84%
First we were not
reluctant to talk.

00:26:55.853 --> 00:26:57.020 align:middle line:90%
You mean you were reluctant.

00:26:57.020 --> 00:26:57.920 align:middle line:90%
Reluctant to talk.

00:26:57.920 --> 00:26:59.105 align:middle line:90%
You were reluctant to talk.

00:26:59.105 --> 00:27:00.480 align:middle line:84%
Reluctant to talk
with strangers.

00:27:00.480 --> 00:27:01.040 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

00:27:01.040 --> 00:27:06.260 align:middle line:84%
And the most talking came
between ourselves, all kinds

00:27:06.260 --> 00:27:07.550 align:middle line:90%
of things between ourselves.

00:27:07.550 --> 00:27:08.800 align:middle line:90%
You mean you with your sister?

00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:10.243 align:middle line:90%
What about these friends?

00:27:10.243 --> 00:27:10.950 align:middle line:90%
Between us.

00:27:10.950 --> 00:27:13.130 align:middle line:84%
Friends from home came
that you knew too.

00:27:13.130 --> 00:27:14.630 align:middle line:90%
Right, yes.

00:27:14.630 --> 00:27:15.500 align:middle line:90%
Fellow survivors.

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:19.550 align:middle line:84%
Why did you decide
to leave Israel?

00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:22.620 align:middle line:84%
Well, it was Israel, I left
Israel because first of all,

00:27:22.620 --> 00:27:23.700 align:middle line:90%
I had no family there.

00:27:23.700 --> 00:27:24.200 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:25.970 align:middle line:84%
You had this sister
naturally there is this--

00:27:25.970 --> 00:27:26.470 align:middle line:90%
this tie.

00:27:26.470 --> 00:27:30.627 align:middle line:84%
And my sister somehow,
she says she felt--

00:27:30.627 --> 00:27:31.460 align:middle line:90%
She wanted somebody.

00:27:31.460 --> 00:27:32.670 align:middle line:90%
She wanted me to be.

00:27:32.670 --> 00:27:33.560 align:middle line:90%
I can understand.

00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:38.210 align:middle line:84%
So and I felt empty in Israel
at holidays and all that.

00:27:38.210 --> 00:27:40.590 align:middle line:84%
OK, I used to have
friends and all of that.

00:27:40.590 --> 00:27:41.840 align:middle line:90%
But still my sister is family.

00:27:41.840 --> 00:27:43.350 align:middle line:90%
Family is family, right.

00:27:43.350 --> 00:27:43.850 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:27:43.850 --> 00:27:47.780 align:middle line:84%
When you came to Cleveland
then, did you join a synagogue?

00:27:47.780 --> 00:27:51.770 align:middle line:84%
Yes, I joined at the time the
Marmarosher Jewish Temple,

00:27:51.770 --> 00:27:55.250 align:middle line:90%
which was on Lancashire.

00:27:55.250 --> 00:27:57.575 align:middle line:84%
That was a Hungarian
congregation.

00:27:57.575 --> 00:28:01.310 align:middle line:84%
Yes, Hungarian congregation,
and till this--

00:28:01.310 --> 00:28:02.900 align:middle line:90%
Why did you join?

00:28:02.900 --> 00:28:04.700 align:middle line:90%
What, the temple?

00:28:04.700 --> 00:28:07.640 align:middle line:84%
Well, because I felt
I'm part of Jewish.

00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:08.210 align:middle line:90%
That's right.

00:28:08.210 --> 00:28:10.460 align:middle line:84%
Your religion meant something,
still meant something.

00:28:10.460 --> 00:28:14.040 align:middle line:84%
Was your rabbi helpful
or comforting in any way?

00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:15.440 align:middle line:90%
We didn't talk with the rabbi.

00:28:15.440 --> 00:28:18.080 align:middle line:84%
We didn't talk with
anybody on that.

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:23.690 align:middle line:84%
All of them was a, so
to speak, we were we.

00:28:23.690 --> 00:28:26.660 align:middle line:84%
The rest of it is
an outside world.

00:28:26.660 --> 00:28:28.160 align:middle line:84%
In other words,
meant nothing to us.

00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:32.230 align:middle line:84%
How did you feel as a
Jew in the United States?

00:28:32.230 --> 00:28:37.000 align:middle line:84%
Well, the one thing that
I liked it, and I still do

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:44.890 align:middle line:84%
is that first of all, that I'm
protected by the Constitution.

00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:48.950 align:middle line:84%
I can go where I want, and when
I want, and do what I want.

00:28:48.950 --> 00:28:51.470 align:middle line:84%
Which, of course,
to us and to me,

00:28:51.470 --> 00:28:53.980 align:middle line:84%
especially, I had the
same thing in Israel.

00:28:53.980 --> 00:28:56.290 align:middle line:90%
But Israel is Israel.

00:28:56.290 --> 00:28:57.730 align:middle line:90%
It's the Jewish state.

00:28:57.730 --> 00:28:59.695 align:middle line:90%
Here, it's not the Jewish state.

00:28:59.695 --> 00:29:01.795 align:middle line:84%
It's different compared
to what was there.

00:29:01.795 --> 00:29:04.960 align:middle line:90%


00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:06.490 align:middle line:90%
Besides, it's America.

00:29:06.490 --> 00:29:09.160 align:middle line:84%
Everybody has the same
rights, and the same thing,

00:29:09.160 --> 00:29:12.490 align:middle line:84%
as long as it's in the framework
of the law and order, which

00:29:12.490 --> 00:29:14.650 align:middle line:90%
is for everybody to obey.

00:29:14.650 --> 00:29:21.200 align:middle line:84%
And nobody's privileged to be
different than anybody else.

00:29:21.200 --> 00:29:21.820 align:middle line:90%
I liked it.

00:29:21.820 --> 00:29:22.420 align:middle line:90%
I loved it.

00:29:22.420 --> 00:29:23.260 align:middle line:90%
It's beautiful.

00:29:23.260 --> 00:29:24.650 align:middle line:90%
No problem about that.

00:29:24.650 --> 00:29:28.750 align:middle line:84%
Can you please tell me how your
Holocaust experiences affect

00:29:28.750 --> 00:29:30.910 align:middle line:90%
you now?

00:29:30.910 --> 00:29:31.600 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:32.900 align:middle line:90%
They do affect me.

00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:40.865 align:middle line:84%
I see humanity and life from
a different perspective.

00:29:40.865 --> 00:29:47.330 align:middle line:84%
You see, from my perspective
America has developed today,

00:29:47.330 --> 00:29:49.540 align:middle line:90%
especially in the--

00:29:49.540 --> 00:29:53.980 align:middle line:84%
I don't know, if it's only
in the Jewish community

00:29:53.980 --> 00:29:58.750 align:middle line:84%
or is it Jewish, issues or
is it Jewish reflections,

00:29:58.750 --> 00:30:00.728 align:middle line:90%
or if it is human reflections.

00:30:00.728 --> 00:30:01.270 align:middle line:90%
I don't know.

00:30:01.270 --> 00:30:03.390 align:middle line:84%
I have never been
anything else but a Jew.

00:30:03.390 --> 00:30:04.000 align:middle line:90%
I understand.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:07.550 align:middle line:84%
So I look at it from the
Jewish point of view.

00:30:07.550 --> 00:30:14.140 align:middle line:84%
And it's not what you
know, it's who you know.

00:30:14.140 --> 00:30:18.710 align:middle line:84%
It not what you stand for
as a man, as a human being.

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.600 align:middle line:90%
It's rather what you--

00:30:20.600 --> 00:30:24.690 align:middle line:84%
and not what you represent,
but rather what you possess.

00:30:24.690 --> 00:30:29.750 align:middle line:84%
So in other words,
it's a different thing.

00:30:29.750 --> 00:30:33.230 align:middle line:84%
Well, do you think that comes
from your Holocaust experience?

00:30:33.230 --> 00:30:34.313 align:middle line:90%
No, no, no, no.

00:30:34.313 --> 00:30:35.480 align:middle line:90%
This is what I'm asking you?

00:30:35.480 --> 00:30:38.880 align:middle line:84%
That's the way I'm looking
at from my point of view,

00:30:38.880 --> 00:30:42.770 align:middle line:84%
the way from my Holocaust
experiences, the way I see.

00:30:42.770 --> 00:30:45.425 align:middle line:84%
That you mean the way
you see people today.

00:30:45.425 --> 00:30:47.120 align:middle line:90%
Humanity.

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:48.050 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:30:48.050 --> 00:30:49.595 align:middle line:90%
Their values are very different.

00:30:49.595 --> 00:30:52.220 align:middle line:84%
Different in a way, in
the way they are dividing.

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:55.040 align:middle line:84%
And something else, there's
a lot of people today.

00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:56.240 align:middle line:90%
Are you cynical?

00:30:56.240 --> 00:30:56.900 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:30:56.900 --> 00:30:57.920 align:middle line:90%
That's a fact.

00:30:57.920 --> 00:30:58.550 align:middle line:90%
Oh, OK.

00:30:58.550 --> 00:30:59.840 align:middle line:90%
That to me it's a fact.

00:30:59.840 --> 00:31:00.920 align:middle line:90%
That it's not.

00:31:00.920 --> 00:31:02.822 align:middle line:84%
To you or to another,
it's an outsider.

00:31:02.822 --> 00:31:04.280 align:middle line:84%
That's what I'm
trying to bring out

00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:06.260 align:middle line:90%
the insider and the outsider.

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:06.980 align:middle line:90%
You see?

00:31:06.980 --> 00:31:09.770 align:middle line:84%
You hear a lot about
the Holocaust today.

00:31:09.770 --> 00:31:11.660 align:middle line:90%
And a lot has been written.

00:31:11.660 --> 00:31:15.530 align:middle line:84%
And probably a lot more will
be written, and a lot of more

00:31:15.530 --> 00:31:16.850 align:middle line:90%
will be discussed.

00:31:16.850 --> 00:31:19.220 align:middle line:84%
And there is no expert
on the Holocaust.

00:31:19.220 --> 00:31:20.900 align:middle line:84%
Because to understand
the Holocaust,

00:31:20.900 --> 00:31:23.900 align:middle line:84%
you've got to look at it only
from three point of views.

00:31:23.900 --> 00:31:27.710 align:middle line:84%
And the one point of
view is what kind of man

00:31:27.710 --> 00:31:31.280 align:middle line:84%
can do that kind of brutality,
or that kind of things

00:31:31.280 --> 00:31:32.550 align:middle line:90%
to another man.

00:31:32.550 --> 00:31:37.850 align:middle line:84%
And then what kind of humanity
has existed at that time that

00:31:37.850 --> 00:31:40.220 align:middle line:90%
permitted itself?

00:31:40.220 --> 00:31:43.290 align:middle line:84%
Permitted between themselves
something like this to happen.

00:31:43.290 --> 00:31:45.950 align:middle line:84%
And then you have to look at it
from the Jewish point of view.

00:31:45.950 --> 00:31:49.010 align:middle line:84%
It's not easy to say
and to point a finger.

00:31:49.010 --> 00:31:53.120 align:middle line:84%
But before you point the
finger, look at yourself

00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:56.690 align:middle line:84%
and say, what have
I not contributed?

00:31:56.690 --> 00:31:58.740 align:middle line:90%
What have I not done?

00:31:58.740 --> 00:32:02.330 align:middle line:84%
And I let myself to be put
in the position where I was.

00:32:02.330 --> 00:32:05.000 align:middle line:84%
So what kind of
Jewish leadership,

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:07.700 align:middle line:84%
what kind of Jewish
existence did I

00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:10.130 align:middle line:84%
have as a Jew at
that particular time

00:32:10.130 --> 00:32:13.250 align:middle line:84%
that I permitted myself
in the framework of what

00:32:13.250 --> 00:32:14.582 align:middle line:90%
happened to be there?

00:32:14.582 --> 00:32:16.040 align:middle line:84%
Did you think you
could control it?

00:32:16.040 --> 00:32:17.075 align:middle line:90%
Yes, we could.

00:32:17.075 --> 00:32:18.450 align:middle line:84%
How could you have
controlled it?

00:32:18.450 --> 00:32:22.480 align:middle line:84%
Well, plain and simply, by if
we had known what's going on,

00:32:22.480 --> 00:32:26.100 align:middle line:84%
we could have not
gone, like resisted.

00:32:26.100 --> 00:32:30.000 align:middle line:84%
But you if you had known what
was going on, you said that--

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.030 align:middle line:84%
If you had more information,
it would have been

00:32:33.030 --> 00:32:35.430 align:middle line:90%
a little bit more organized.

00:32:35.430 --> 00:32:37.290 align:middle line:84%
We could have had
the resistance.

00:32:37.290 --> 00:32:39.320 align:middle line:84%
There were pockets
of resistance.

00:32:39.320 --> 00:32:40.870 align:middle line:84%
The Warsaw ghetto
was resistance.

00:32:40.870 --> 00:32:41.370 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

00:32:41.370 --> 00:32:44.190 align:middle line:84%
And yes, the Germans
paid a price for it.

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:45.420 align:middle line:90%
They didn't took it easy.

00:32:45.420 --> 00:32:47.770 align:middle line:84%
In Budapest, there
was resistance.

00:32:47.770 --> 00:32:50.640 align:middle line:84%
I remember being a part of a
group going out to the streets

00:32:50.640 --> 00:32:52.500 align:middle line:84%
and we observed,
and we saw Germans

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:55.770 align:middle line:84%
that the youth, the
Hakenkreuz youth,

00:32:55.770 --> 00:32:59.330 align:middle line:84%
which the German Hakenkreuz
youth who call themselves.

00:32:59.330 --> 00:33:03.090 align:middle line:84%
We used to go over, I remember
it positively, and definitely,

00:33:03.090 --> 00:33:05.770 align:middle line:90%
and extremely well.

00:33:05.770 --> 00:33:09.062 align:middle line:84%
We run over to those kids, and
we said, hey, you're Jewish.

00:33:09.062 --> 00:33:10.770 align:middle line:84%
They said, what do
you mean you're a Jew.

00:33:10.770 --> 00:33:11.740 align:middle line:90%
I'm not Jewish.

00:33:11.740 --> 00:33:13.440 align:middle line:90%
I said you're a Jew.

00:33:13.440 --> 00:33:15.450 align:middle line:90%
We had the same Hakenkreuz on.

00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:16.750 align:middle line:90%
We spoke their language.

00:33:16.750 --> 00:33:18.395 align:middle line:90%
And we said you're Jewish.

00:33:18.395 --> 00:33:21.020 align:middle line:84%
And then we took them underneath
to show that they are not Jew.

00:33:21.020 --> 00:33:23.478 align:middle line:84%
They let their pants down and
prove that you're not Jewish.

00:33:23.478 --> 00:33:25.712 align:middle line:84%
And then we beat the hell
out of them right there.

00:33:25.712 --> 00:33:27.920 align:middle line:84%
There were incidents already
killed them right there.

00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:31.170 align:middle line:84%
So there was all kind
of way of resistance.

00:33:31.170 --> 00:33:32.960 align:middle line:84%
But when you see
in those frameworks

00:33:32.960 --> 00:33:35.870 align:middle line:84%
and the way things
have been, you see,

00:33:35.870 --> 00:33:38.510 align:middle line:90%
that's the way it happened.

00:33:38.510 --> 00:33:41.300 align:middle line:84%
How often do you talk
about the Holocaust?

00:33:41.300 --> 00:33:43.670 align:middle line:84%
Well, we mostly
between ourselves

00:33:43.670 --> 00:33:45.560 align:middle line:84%
we talk very often,
almost every time.

00:33:45.560 --> 00:33:46.773 align:middle line:90%
You have lots of friends.

00:33:46.773 --> 00:33:47.690 align:middle line:90%
With the friends, yes.

00:33:47.690 --> 00:33:48.440 align:middle line:90%
Survivors.

00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:55.460 align:middle line:84%
But it's always we
will remain no matter

00:33:55.460 --> 00:33:59.990 align:middle line:84%
what anybody says, no matter
how fancy he sees himself,

00:33:59.990 --> 00:34:07.070 align:middle line:84%
and nice words or
plain words, we will

00:34:07.070 --> 00:34:09.560 align:middle line:90%
remain on outside of humanity.

00:34:09.560 --> 00:34:13.100 align:middle line:84%
We can never be
part of the humanity

00:34:13.100 --> 00:34:16.489 align:middle line:84%
as in the way with
this experience.

00:34:16.489 --> 00:34:17.659 align:middle line:90%
There is always--

00:34:17.659 --> 00:34:19.365 align:middle line:84%
You think it's
affected your whole.

00:34:19.365 --> 00:34:20.017 align:middle line:90%
Absolutely.

00:34:20.017 --> 00:34:22.350 align:middle line:84%
And everybody, you think it's
affected the way everybody

00:34:22.350 --> 00:34:23.610 align:middle line:90%
looks at you.

00:34:23.610 --> 00:34:24.540 align:middle line:90%
No, no, no, no, no.

00:34:24.540 --> 00:34:25.830 align:middle line:90%
No, no, not in that sense.

00:34:25.830 --> 00:34:27.760 align:middle line:84%
And I'm talking all
of the survivors.

00:34:27.760 --> 00:34:28.260 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:34:28.260 --> 00:34:30.360 align:middle line:90%
They are all at the same.

00:34:30.360 --> 00:34:32.949 align:middle line:84%
No matter what they say,
one way or the other,

00:34:32.949 --> 00:34:35.190 align:middle line:90%
that's the way the feelings.

00:34:35.190 --> 00:34:36.060 align:middle line:90%
And that's the way--

00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:38.565 align:middle line:84%
You think it's affected your
whole social relationship

00:34:38.565 --> 00:34:39.190 align:middle line:90%
with everybody.

00:34:39.190 --> 00:34:39.690 align:middle line:90%
Absolutely.

00:34:39.690 --> 00:34:44.268 align:middle line:84%
We look at man, of our fellow
men from a different angle,

00:34:44.268 --> 00:34:49.770 align:middle line:84%
from a different point of
view, and from a different--

00:34:49.770 --> 00:34:51.330 align:middle line:90%
with all the knowledge.

00:34:51.330 --> 00:34:53.980 align:middle line:84%
So you think that survivors
are different from other Jews?

00:34:53.980 --> 00:34:54.480 align:middle line:90%
Absolutely.

00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:56.340 align:middle line:90%
How?

00:34:56.340 --> 00:35:01.870 align:middle line:90%
It's their own feeling.

00:35:01.870 --> 00:35:09.940 align:middle line:84%
It's there inside by paying a
commendous humanly impossible

00:35:09.940 --> 00:35:13.780 align:middle line:84%
to explain in words,
the price they paid

00:35:13.780 --> 00:35:16.810 align:middle line:90%
in order for their Jewishness.

00:35:16.810 --> 00:35:22.060 align:middle line:84%
So therefore, you look on it of
their being of this Jewishness.

00:35:22.060 --> 00:35:25.180 align:middle line:84%
Of course, whatever
experiences any of us

00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:28.720 align:middle line:84%
go through affect our
behavior and our thoughts.

00:35:28.720 --> 00:35:30.220 align:middle line:84%
I can understand
what you're saying.

00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:34.690 align:middle line:84%
OK, now you see, it affects if
somebody survives an accident,

00:35:34.690 --> 00:35:36.280 align:middle line:90%
a car accident.

00:35:36.280 --> 00:35:38.230 align:middle line:90%
Somebody survives an illness.

00:35:38.230 --> 00:35:39.440 align:middle line:90%
Sure, it affects their life.

00:35:39.440 --> 00:35:39.940 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:44.410 align:middle line:84%
It affects in different things
affect us in different ways.

00:35:44.410 --> 00:35:45.190 align:middle line:90%
That's true.

00:35:45.190 --> 00:35:49.090 align:middle line:84%
And this-- but when we have been
abused, for months and years,

00:35:49.090 --> 00:35:52.510 align:middle line:84%
in everyday life, and
in everyday happenings,

00:35:52.510 --> 00:35:57.070 align:middle line:90%
it's a story in itself.

00:35:57.070 --> 00:36:02.490 align:middle line:84%
And it's each one, even
individually locks his own,

00:36:02.490 --> 00:36:06.740 align:middle line:84%
so to speak lock, and
looks for his own key

00:36:06.740 --> 00:36:08.210 align:middle line:90%
to open up that particular.

00:36:08.210 --> 00:36:11.000 align:middle line:84%
Larry, do you think there are
any reasons for your survival?

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:14.690 align:middle line:90%
Do you ever think about that?

00:36:14.690 --> 00:36:18.440 align:middle line:84%
Is there any reason
why you survived?

00:36:18.440 --> 00:36:21.920 align:middle line:90%
I don't know if the reason--

00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:27.710 align:middle line:84%
a reason is-- this is
a question beyond me.

00:36:27.710 --> 00:36:31.220 align:middle line:84%
Because they are factors
which are beyond my control

00:36:31.220 --> 00:36:32.450 align:middle line:90%
in order to be able--

00:36:32.450 --> 00:36:35.000 align:middle line:84%
You don't think
it was just luck?

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:38.420 align:middle line:84%
I can speak only from
the human point of view.

00:36:38.420 --> 00:36:41.138 align:middle line:84%
No, I'm asking about your
point of view, from you.

00:36:41.138 --> 00:36:41.930 align:middle line:90%
That's what I mean.

00:36:41.930 --> 00:36:42.710 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:36:42.710 --> 00:36:45.320 align:middle line:84%
From mine, as a human being,
from my own human being point

00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:45.820 align:middle line:90%
of view--

00:36:45.820 --> 00:36:46.370 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:36:46.370 --> 00:36:50.600 align:middle line:84%
Going beyond the mysticism
and all of that, from my,

00:36:50.600 --> 00:36:54.920 align:middle line:84%
it was involved two
things, the will of power

00:36:54.920 --> 00:36:58.280 align:middle line:90%
to survive no matter what.

00:36:58.280 --> 00:36:59.570 align:middle line:90%
Age, I was young.

00:36:59.570 --> 00:37:00.920 align:middle line:90%
I could take the abuse.

00:37:00.920 --> 00:37:02.850 align:middle line:84%
I could stand it
and all of that.

00:37:02.850 --> 00:37:04.788 align:middle line:90%
And to cope with it.

00:37:04.788 --> 00:37:06.830 align:middle line:84%
To cope with the circumstances
and to cope with--

00:37:06.830 --> 00:37:08.600 align:middle line:90%
Your resourcefulness.

00:37:08.600 --> 00:37:11.660 align:middle line:84%
And that is the main
thing for the survival.

00:37:11.660 --> 00:37:16.040 align:middle line:84%
And then there is
an element of luck.

00:37:16.040 --> 00:37:19.640 align:middle line:84%
To be, so to speak, what we
say today in our modern terms,

00:37:19.640 --> 00:37:21.630 align:middle line:84%
of being at the right
place in the right time.

00:37:21.630 --> 00:37:22.130 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:37:22.130 --> 00:37:27.290 align:middle line:84%
And that made a lot of to
do with many survivors.

00:37:27.290 --> 00:37:27.900 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:37:27.900 --> 00:37:29.630 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:37:29.630 --> 00:37:31.760 align:middle line:84%
What thoughts do you
have now when you

00:37:31.760 --> 00:37:33.095 align:middle line:90%
remember what you went through?

00:37:33.095 --> 00:37:36.440 align:middle line:90%


00:37:36.440 --> 00:37:38.330 align:middle line:90%
Stupidity of humanity.

00:37:38.330 --> 00:37:42.110 align:middle line:90%


00:37:42.110 --> 00:37:43.595 align:middle line:90%
Do we ever going to learn?

00:37:43.595 --> 00:37:46.310 align:middle line:90%


00:37:46.310 --> 00:37:51.350 align:middle line:84%
There are so many wise men said
so many statements, so many

00:37:51.350 --> 00:37:54.200 align:middle line:90%
fancy words.

00:37:54.200 --> 00:38:00.830 align:middle line:84%
Like the guy who said, if you
don't learn from our mistakes,

00:38:00.830 --> 00:38:03.440 align:middle line:90%
we are bound to regret.

00:38:03.440 --> 00:38:06.860 align:middle line:84%
I forgot the name of the
philosopher who said that.

00:38:06.860 --> 00:38:09.650 align:middle line:84%
Now how many times have
you learned already

00:38:09.650 --> 00:38:11.520 align:middle line:90%
throughout history?

00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:17.150 align:middle line:84%
And how many times have people,
nations, and all regret?

00:38:17.150 --> 00:38:21.830 align:middle line:84%
Are we learning the consequences
from it, till this day?

00:38:21.830 --> 00:38:25.220 align:middle line:84%
Is man's inhumanity
towards man changed?

00:38:25.220 --> 00:38:26.330 align:middle line:90%
We know about it.

00:38:26.330 --> 00:38:27.950 align:middle line:90%
Right, right, right.

00:38:27.950 --> 00:38:30.860 align:middle line:84%
And in fact, with
all those development

00:38:30.860 --> 00:38:37.500 align:middle line:84%
of new weapons and new
stuff, more destructive,

00:38:37.500 --> 00:38:43.020 align:middle line:84%
more terrible, with
more pain and tears

00:38:43.020 --> 00:38:44.550 align:middle line:90%
to inflict on each other.

00:38:44.550 --> 00:38:48.540 align:middle line:84%
And start to find ways
to co-exist and to exist

00:38:48.540 --> 00:38:50.610 align:middle line:90%
and to better for ourselves.

00:38:50.610 --> 00:38:53.370 align:middle line:84%
Larry, do you think
that survivors

00:38:53.370 --> 00:38:57.180 align:middle line:84%
have a message that
others need to understand?

00:38:57.180 --> 00:38:59.970 align:middle line:90%


00:38:59.970 --> 00:39:04.380 align:middle line:84%
The survivors have
more than a message.

00:39:04.380 --> 00:39:09.180 align:middle line:84%
And I'm coming to
conclusion to believe

00:39:09.180 --> 00:39:14.130 align:middle line:84%
that a problem is because it's
looked on us like a message.

00:39:14.130 --> 00:39:16.290 align:middle line:90%
And it's more than a message.

00:39:16.290 --> 00:39:18.510 align:middle line:90%
It's not a message.

00:39:18.510 --> 00:39:22.620 align:middle line:84%
It's when I said before in the
[? readings. ?] You remember?

00:39:22.620 --> 00:39:26.220 align:middle line:84%
On what kind of
humanity existed.

00:39:26.220 --> 00:39:30.030 align:middle line:84%
The same humanity exists
today with a little bit

00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:34.320 align:middle line:84%
more knowledge, and with a
little bit more know-how.

00:39:34.320 --> 00:39:40.920 align:middle line:84%
But we don't have the power more
than to bring it across to you

00:39:40.920 --> 00:39:44.220 align:middle line:84%
and telling you of
what you, humanity, are

00:39:44.220 --> 00:39:48.120 align:middle line:90%
capable in doing to yourself.

00:39:48.120 --> 00:39:49.440 align:middle line:90%
And what good is it?

00:39:49.440 --> 00:39:50.850 align:middle line:90%
We are bringing it across.

00:39:50.850 --> 00:39:52.900 align:middle line:90%
We are trying to tell you.

00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:56.040 align:middle line:84%
Nobody came down
from outer space

00:39:56.040 --> 00:39:58.560 align:middle line:84%
and did to us what
has been done.

00:39:58.560 --> 00:40:01.890 align:middle line:84%
Only human beings from
here who arrived here

00:40:01.890 --> 00:40:04.980 align:middle line:84%
in the same way we did,
who live in the same way.

00:40:04.980 --> 00:40:09.600 align:middle line:84%
As here as Jews,
as Jewish people,

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:13.530 align:middle line:84%
for generations we have been
telling the non-Jewish world,

00:40:13.530 --> 00:40:15.030 align:middle line:90%
look.

00:40:15.030 --> 00:40:18.600 align:middle line:84%
When we are sick, we need
a doctor and medicine.

00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:21.810 align:middle line:84%
When we are hungry,
we need food.

00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:25.870 align:middle line:84%
When we are cold, we need
clothing and shelter.

00:40:25.870 --> 00:40:28.800 align:middle line:84%
We have beautiful
looking women, so do you.

00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:30.360 align:middle line:90%
We have great athletes.

00:40:30.360 --> 00:40:31.440 align:middle line:90%
So do you.

00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:32.820 align:middle line:90%
We have wise men.

00:40:32.820 --> 00:40:33.750 align:middle line:90%
So do you.

00:40:33.750 --> 00:40:35.010 align:middle line:90%
We have stupid men.

00:40:35.010 --> 00:40:35.730 align:middle line:90%
So do you.

00:40:35.730 --> 00:40:38.370 align:middle line:84%
So we are not
differently than you are.

00:40:38.370 --> 00:40:43.590 align:middle line:84%
Yet, at every so
often, we are getting

00:40:43.590 --> 00:40:45.660 align:middle line:84%
trodden down and
down to us what has

00:40:45.660 --> 00:40:47.190 align:middle line:90%
been done throughout history.

00:40:47.190 --> 00:40:50.820 align:middle line:90%
But it's repeating itself.

00:40:50.820 --> 00:40:54.450 align:middle line:84%
Every time, every so
often, and humanity

00:40:54.450 --> 00:40:56.880 align:middle line:90%
does not want to accept.

00:40:56.880 --> 00:40:58.800 align:middle line:90%
Or they do not want to listen.

00:40:58.800 --> 00:41:03.861 align:middle line:90%


00:41:03.861 --> 00:41:08.730 align:middle line:84%
Well, in your opinion, what
would be an appropriate way

00:41:08.730 --> 00:41:11.910 align:middle line:84%
to commemorate the
memory of those

00:41:11.910 --> 00:41:16.210 align:middle line:84%
who lost their lives
during the Holocaust years?

00:41:16.210 --> 00:41:21.400 align:middle line:84%
The best way to commemorate
is first of all,

00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:25.410 align:middle line:84%
let's not make out
of it a Jewish issue.

00:41:25.410 --> 00:41:29.620 align:middle line:90%
We were Jews, the victims.

00:41:29.620 --> 00:41:32.460 align:middle line:90%
Let's make it a human issue.

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:34.980 align:middle line:84%
Well, there were
many more than Jews

00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:37.560 align:middle line:84%
who died during the
Holocaust years, right?

00:41:37.560 --> 00:41:38.060 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:39.020 align:middle line:90%
This is what you're telling me.

00:41:39.020 --> 00:41:39.340 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:41:39.340 --> 00:41:39.840 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:40.940 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:41:40.940 --> 00:41:44.780 align:middle line:84%
Exactly right,
But the difference

00:41:44.780 --> 00:41:47.480 align:middle line:90%
between the two of them is this.

00:41:47.480 --> 00:41:55.730 align:middle line:84%
If you were Polish, French,
Czech, or whatever nationality,

00:41:55.730 --> 00:41:58.040 align:middle line:90%
you lived in your own country.

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:00.530 align:middle line:84%
If you obey the
rules and the laws

00:42:00.530 --> 00:42:04.130 align:middle line:84%
of the occupational
force, most of the time

00:42:04.130 --> 00:42:06.200 align:middle line:90%
they didn't bother you.

00:42:06.200 --> 00:42:08.510 align:middle line:84%
You could have a
chance to survive.

00:42:08.510 --> 00:42:11.960 align:middle line:84%
But with us, we didn't
have this chance.

00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:13.550 align:middle line:90%
We were Jews.

00:42:13.550 --> 00:42:16.370 align:middle line:84%
And as a Jew, you were
condemned automatically,

00:42:16.370 --> 00:42:20.870 align:middle line:84%
no matter what your beliefs are,
and in what country you live.

00:42:20.870 --> 00:42:23.090 align:middle line:84%
You were automatically
condemned.

00:42:23.090 --> 00:42:24.650 align:middle line:90%
That makes the difference.

00:42:24.650 --> 00:42:25.640 align:middle line:90%
That's number one.

00:42:25.640 --> 00:42:33.660 align:middle line:84%
And number two, it was a
Christian world around us

00:42:33.660 --> 00:42:35.130 align:middle line:90%
what did happen.

00:42:35.130 --> 00:42:43.450 align:middle line:84%
And let Christianity understand
that their indifference is not

00:42:43.450 --> 00:42:45.620 align:middle line:90%
the answer.

00:42:45.620 --> 00:42:48.610 align:middle line:84%
There were many Christian
leaders who stood up,

00:42:48.610 --> 00:42:50.020 align:middle line:90%
no question on that.

00:42:50.020 --> 00:42:53.140 align:middle line:90%
But they were in a minority.

00:42:53.140 --> 00:42:55.510 align:middle line:90%
And their voice wasn't heard.

00:42:55.510 --> 00:42:58.090 align:middle line:84%
They were not even
permitted to listen.

00:42:58.090 --> 00:43:01.600 align:middle line:84%
So countries where freedom of
speech and freedom of action

00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:05.890 align:middle line:84%
in everything is
free and possible,

00:43:05.890 --> 00:43:07.850 align:middle line:84%
they should stand
up and be heard.

00:43:07.850 --> 00:43:11.500 align:middle line:84%
And this is where
we survivors have

00:43:11.500 --> 00:43:13.390 align:middle line:90%
to bring across the message.

00:43:13.390 --> 00:43:16.900 align:middle line:84%
To understand what
it can be done.

00:43:16.900 --> 00:43:21.100 align:middle line:84%
I heard today from Jews,
my own Jewish people,

00:43:21.100 --> 00:43:23.860 align:middle line:84%
saying that a religious
Jew wouldn't touch it

00:43:23.860 --> 00:43:26.620 align:middle line:90%
with a 10 foot pole.

00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:27.677 align:middle line:90%
It's not right.

00:43:27.677 --> 00:43:28.510 align:middle line:90%
I didn't understand.

00:43:28.510 --> 00:43:32.420 align:middle line:84%
A Jew, religious Jews don't want
to talk about the Holocaust.

00:43:32.420 --> 00:43:32.920 align:middle line:90%
Why?

00:43:32.920 --> 00:43:37.540 align:middle line:84%
Because their belief is
that it was God's doing.

00:43:37.540 --> 00:43:39.580 align:middle line:90%
What God had to do with it?

00:43:39.580 --> 00:43:41.440 align:middle line:90%
I don't buy that.

00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:43.940 align:middle line:90%
God didn't create the Holocaust.

00:43:43.940 --> 00:43:47.240 align:middle line:84%
It was man's
inhumanity towards man.

00:43:47.240 --> 00:43:48.710 align:middle line:90%
It wasn't God.

00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:52.130 align:middle line:84%
There are Christians I heard
many times Christianity saying,

00:43:52.130 --> 00:43:54.770 align:middle line:90%
learn to forgive and to forget.

00:43:54.770 --> 00:43:56.480 align:middle line:90%
I cannot forget.

00:43:56.480 --> 00:43:57.170 align:middle line:90%
Of course not.

00:43:57.170 --> 00:44:00.320 align:middle line:84%
And to forgive, it's not a
question of me, will I forgive,

00:44:00.320 --> 00:44:03.200 align:middle line:84%
of me Larry Hersh, as a
Jew and as a survivor.

00:44:03.200 --> 00:44:07.280 align:middle line:84%
The question is,
would Jesus the Jew

00:44:07.280 --> 00:44:09.950 align:middle line:90%
forgive them for their silence?

00:44:09.950 --> 00:44:12.950 align:middle line:90%
It's not me.

00:44:12.950 --> 00:44:15.540 align:middle line:84%
What good is the
entire Christianity?

00:44:15.540 --> 00:44:21.270 align:middle line:84%
As when the chips are down
and when his teachings count,

00:44:21.270 --> 00:44:22.700 align:middle line:90%
they're not there.

00:44:22.700 --> 00:44:25.370 align:middle line:84%
I have one, just one
further question, Larry.

00:44:25.370 --> 00:44:30.110 align:middle line:84%
In what ways can those of
us who are not survivors

00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:33.020 align:middle line:84%
relate to those of
you who went through

00:44:33.020 --> 00:44:35.000 align:middle line:90%
these terrible experiences?

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:40.130 align:middle line:84%
Do you expect is there anything
that we, as caring and humane

00:44:40.130 --> 00:44:46.530 align:middle line:84%
people, can do to relate to
you and your experiences?

00:44:46.530 --> 00:44:48.770 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:44:48.770 --> 00:44:50.690 align:middle line:84%
The only way a
relationship can be

00:44:50.690 --> 00:44:59.130 align:middle line:84%
is that you understand
what we went through,

00:44:59.130 --> 00:45:06.810 align:middle line:84%
show that you have their
human, show understanding

00:45:06.810 --> 00:45:11.610 align:middle line:84%
because remember, the majority
of us I happen to be lucky

00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:13.080 align:middle line:90%
that I have a sister.

00:45:13.080 --> 00:45:15.050 align:middle line:90%
But the majority without--

00:45:15.050 --> 00:45:15.690 align:middle line:90%
Without anyone.

00:45:15.690 --> 00:45:18.450 align:middle line:90%
--anybody or anything.

00:45:18.450 --> 00:45:21.420 align:middle line:84%
Be honest and let's
look the facts.

00:45:21.420 --> 00:45:24.660 align:middle line:84%
How many people do
you know that have

00:45:24.660 --> 00:45:30.720 align:middle line:84%
invited a survivor just to
come over and say, hey hello.

00:45:30.720 --> 00:45:34.410 align:middle line:84%
Come over on a holiday,
on a Jewish holiday.

00:45:34.410 --> 00:45:39.240 align:middle line:84%
Let's spend a Pesach
one evening with us,

00:45:39.240 --> 00:45:41.940 align:middle line:90%
spend a holiday with us.

00:45:41.940 --> 00:45:44.190 align:middle line:84%
How many families
like this do you know?

00:45:44.190 --> 00:45:44.820 align:middle line:90%
I don't.

00:45:44.820 --> 00:45:47.310 align:middle line:90%
And I have never heard of it.

00:45:47.310 --> 00:45:51.030 align:middle line:84%
The bridges between the Jewish
communities and the survivors,

00:45:51.030 --> 00:45:54.640 align:middle line:84%
and for this matter
even with humanity,

00:45:54.640 --> 00:45:56.310 align:middle line:90%
has never been crossed.

00:45:56.310 --> 00:45:58.140 align:middle line:90%
Now, it's obvious what happened.

00:45:58.140 --> 00:45:59.660 align:middle line:90%
It happened to him.

00:45:59.660 --> 00:46:02.380 align:middle line:90%
He is from somewhere else.

00:46:02.380 --> 00:46:05.230 align:middle line:90%
And this is still this day.

00:46:05.230 --> 00:46:08.690 align:middle line:84%
Well, your story has
been fascinating.

00:46:08.690 --> 00:46:11.870 align:middle line:84%
And we much, much appreciate
your telling it to us.

00:46:11.870 --> 00:46:13.030 align:middle line:90%
More than welcome.

00:46:13.030 --> 00:46:13.630 align:middle line:90%
I just--

00:46:13.630 --> 00:46:14.130 align:middle line:90%
Thank you.

00:46:14.130 --> 00:46:16.150 align:middle line:90%
Thank you so very, very much.

00:46:16.150 --> 00:46:19.630 align:middle line:84%
I just hope that
what I have told

00:46:19.630 --> 00:46:22.840 align:middle line:84%
the future generations
will be able to draw

00:46:22.840 --> 00:46:26.950 align:middle line:84%
the consequences from it, and
understand that there is only

00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:30.430 align:middle line:84%
like we Jews say, there's one
God, and there's one humanity.

00:46:30.430 --> 00:46:31.540 align:middle line:90%
And that's--

00:46:31.540 --> 00:46:33.070 align:middle line:90%
That's the lesson to be learned.

00:46:33.070 --> 00:46:34.060 align:middle line:90%
And that's the must.

00:46:34.060 --> 00:46:36.640 align:middle line:90%
And if somebody gets--

00:46:36.640 --> 00:46:41.530 align:middle line:84%
if any man of any religion,
of any race, or of any color

00:46:41.530 --> 00:46:45.880 align:middle line:84%
is getting depressed or
is suffering depression

00:46:45.880 --> 00:46:48.640 align:middle line:84%
for no other reason than
just for being what he is,

00:46:48.640 --> 00:46:52.480 align:middle line:84%
humanity must stand
up and speak up.

00:46:52.480 --> 00:46:57.340 align:middle line:84%
And this is the only way we
ever survive as a humanity.

00:46:57.340 --> 00:46:57.910 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:46:57.910 --> 00:46:59.328 align:middle line:90%
Again, many, many thanks.

00:46:59.328 --> 00:47:00.370 align:middle line:90%
You're more than welcome.

00:47:00.370 --> 00:47:04.030 align:middle line:84%
It's a beautiful
contribution to our archives.

00:47:04.030 --> 00:47:06.180 align:middle line:90%
Thank you very much.

00:47:06.180 --> 00:47:34.000 align:middle line:90%